# README Maintenance

`README.md` is the canonical project overview. Update it **in the same commit** as the code change whenever any of the following happen:

## When to update

| Change | Section to update |
|---|---|
| New crate added to `crates/` | Project Structure table + Dependency Graph |
| Crate removed or renamed | Project Structure table + Dependency Graph |
| New view type added to `split_view` | Key Concepts → Split-Pane Layout |
| New top-level directory added | Project Structure tree |
| Tech stack dependency added/removed | Tech Stack table |
| Major feature lands (new UI panel, new engine, new CDM block, …) | Key Concepts or Roadmap |
| Phase milestone completed | Roadmap table (✅ / 🔜) |
| Build or run instructions change | Build & Run section |
| New dev convention established | Development → Conventions |

## What NOT to change

- Don't rewrite the Vision or Architecture Principles sections without explicit instruction — those reflect intentional product decisions.
- Don't add implementation details that belong in `docs/` or inline code comments.

## Format rules

- Keep the README scannable: tables over prose wherever possible.
- Crate descriptions in the Project Structure table: one line, present-tense verb phrase (e.g. "Virtualized spreadsheet grid renderer").
- Dependency graph uses ASCII art arrows — keep it updated but don't over-engineer it.
